ies  friends of friends like very few of them  work in tech  and that's a very different from the bay  area where it's like everybody  and their boyfriend partner neighbor  sisters dogs husbands whatever  was working in tech so in that sense i'm  actually very grateful  because tech was everywhere like i like  having the option to be able to seek  things out but when it's like right  there in front of you all the time  you can get kind of old in the bay area  it was really common for people to be  like hey what's your name  what do you do what company do you work  at and like i remember  my first couple of interactions in san  diego where i like  met new people they didn't ask me that  at all like we would talk for like an  hour or two  and they wouldn't ask me what i do and i  was like whoa  this is strange so it's kind of been  really refreshing because it's nice to  be seen for me than  being seen for the work that i do i  guess like that's one really extreme way  to think about it  it does start feeling a little bit like  the company you work out where your role  defines you more than  your behavior or what you say or if  you're funny  or if you're fun to be with what your  other interests are so  that's been super duper refreshing the  other thing that in reflecting about  living in san diego  that's been really nice is that it's  really nice to live like where  your people are granted like my parents  are are no longer in san diego they  moved away to japan  but i saw a lot of friends here from  college and high school  that like coming back it definitely  didn't feel like i had to  move to a new city like we didn't have  to like create new friend groups  just kind of fell back into routine with  like all the friends that we already did  have granted we didn't keep in touch  with everybody because everyone grows  differently and goes their separate ways  but we've like we've kind of picked up  our friendship where  a lot of them left off and that's been  really nice  the other thing in reflecting this last  year is that  it's really nice to live somewhere where  it's just like it matches your lifestyle  i think  a lot like i realized i didn't realize  this was something that was so important  to us but just like  living in a place that matches who you  are and where you're at um and how you  want to spend your time  is so nice like scott and i we generally  like  like going outside enjoying the sun we  like hanging out with nice people  meeting nice strangers we are very like  sunny type of people we get energy from  the sun when it's gloomy for too long we  get kind of like  sad and like it's there's just a whole  lot of stuff  to do in san diego and to eat in san  diego that we enjoy  like we really like mexican food we  really like like the fresh californian  kind of food  there's decently good asian food in san  diego and definitely lots of good asian  food in los angeles the activities here  too it's like  we love going to the beach we love going  to coffee we love going to  fun restaurants with friends we love  going to brunch the lifestyle here  we were talking the other day really  matches who we are and that's  really nice i think like the bay area  definitely it's like i think part of it  is you  you molds you meld to  the lifestyle that you are in or like  the environment that you're in right now  so you know when i was like when i was  living in the bay area it was like you  go to concerts you go to art galleries  you go to bakeries you go to cafes you  go to san francisco  and go on a lot of hikes and that was  really fun too and i really enjoyed my  time there but  i think this is really what's natural  for me it's really one of those things  that i'm like i really took this for  granted going up here  but i'm really glad that i don't take it  for granted now  the last thing that i will say i think  in reflecting this last year is that i  know i've changed a lot  like i think i'm more chill than i used  to 